  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Economy Framework and Model for Malaysia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the assignment is to develop two main outputs, namely the Green Economy Framework and a dynamic Green Economy model for Malaysia. The Green Economy Framework is expected to detail a national Green Economy vision, as well as the extent of the country&#x2019;s economic, environmental, and social readiness to transition to a green economy. Concurrently, the Green Economy model aims to capture baseline conditions in the economy considering climate and natural resource variables, and scenario simulation analysis on impacts of climate change risks and specific policy options that can be used to simulate intervention impacts and provide guidance for macroeconomic planning to achieve national development plans and Net Zero commitments. The project&#x2019;s deliverables will result in a policy tool to provide evidence and analytical inputs in the formulation process of national development plans such as the 13th Malaysia Plan and prioritize macroeconomic policy responses relevant to accelerate the transition towards an inclusive and sustainable future.</narrative>
  </description>
